WEBVTT

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.110
<i>It's been half a month since 
I started working at Étranger.</i>

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.110
<i>I'm responsible for odd jobs...</i>

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.580
<i>and preparing royal milk tea 
the way Richard taught me.</i>

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.370
Bonjour.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.020
Comment allez-vous?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.870
Je suis Richard.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.380
Hao jiu bu jian.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.380
Mama obava dae aekima mage gauravaya.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.690
Ana'atatalae liruyatik maratan ukhraa.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.710
<i>A French woman, a Chinese man,
 and an Arabian... king?</i>

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.310
<i>Just how many languages does he speak?</i>

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:46.850
Richard, I've never seen 
clothes like that up close before.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.440
Isn't he hot in that?

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.690
Seigi, do you remember our agreement?

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.980
Our agreement?

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.140
I know I went over it 
with you when I hired you.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.080
You will exhibit no prejudice 
based on race, religion,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.080
sexual orientation, nationality, 
nor any other criterion,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.920
and you will not speak in 
a discriminatory manner.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.370
That was it!

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.310
No pointing at people.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.930
Sorry.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.880
Be mindful that you aren't 
rude to our customers.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.220
Yes, sir.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:18.220
Also...

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.470
Don't be stingy with the tea leaves.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.980
Sorry.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.030
<u>Episode 2</u>
<b>The Ruby's Truth</b>

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.320
Welcome.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:15.590
Hello. You're open, right?

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.960
Do I need an appointment?

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.800
The manager is a foreigner?

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:25.260
Welcome. What can I do for you?

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:29.020
Your Japanese is quite good.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.480
Thank you.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.670
I'm the owner, 
Richard Ranashinha de Vulpian.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.320
I'm... Akashi Mami.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.380
Now, what can I do for you?

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:49.790
I'd like you to appraise this.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.670
If I may...

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.550
A lot of rubies are warmed up, right?

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.980
You're talking about the process
 known as heat treatment, yes?

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:18.770
I'd like you to determine if this 
ruby has been heated or not.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:24.780
In that case, you'd like me to valuate 
only the ruby and not the diamonds?

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.150
Yes, just that.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:29.030
Understood.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.330
<b>Request Form

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.280
Well, then, I'll contact you
 once I have the results.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.960
Thank you.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.410
She seemed to be in a hurry.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:52.240
This is the ruby, huh?

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.360
It's so red.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:59.830
It's the color of the speck 
of blood you see in chicken.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:04.150
Is that a joke? Or do you actually 
know what you're talking about?

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.530
What do you mean?

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.280
"Pigeon blood."

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.670
Pigeon... blood?

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.620
Yes.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.190
It's a term used to describe rubies 
found only in certain mines in Myanmar.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.920
They're of the highest quality
 and the brightest red.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.550
But if you said that without knowing...

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:25.670
Good for you.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.030
Good... What?

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.020
Was that a compliment?

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.430
Thank you.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.140
Oh, she forgot something!

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.710
I'd better take it to her.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:38.910
Seigi...

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.150
I'll be back!

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.340
There she is.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.700
Ma'am!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.600
Ma'am!

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.760
Here. You forgot this.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.440
Thank you.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.480
Um... Are you all right?

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.420
Did you find Akashi-san?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.460
She was making the face my grandma used to...

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.500
She was acting a little strange.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.300
Her request was also a little unusual.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:49.930
Huh?

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:55.010
It's rare for someone to ask if a 
gemstone has been heated or not.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.880
What's this about heating?

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.780
Heat treatment.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.880
In the case of rubies and sapphires,

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.440
heating them brightens their color.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.170
Really? So there's a chemical reaction.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.740
Yes. Now it's time for a little quiz.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:19.250
Between a drably colored unheated ruby 
and a clear red heated ruby,

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.750
which is more valuable?

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:26.500
This one's prettier, but... the unheated one?

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.960
Too bad.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.380
What?

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.470
Its beauty is what matters.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.880
Most rubies on the market are heated.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.690
Really?

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:39.500
That said, when it comes 
to pigeon blood rubies,

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.470
the natural, unheated gemstones 
are more expensive.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:47.330
However, suppose a ruby was 
discovered after a death in your family.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:50.360
Would you be worried about whether 
or not it had been heat-treated?

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.570
No. It's still a valuable gemstone.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.660
That's right.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.440
It's rare for people to care,

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.140
and even rarer for them to come ask about it.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.290
Then why did Akashi-san?

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:11.840
In general, people are concerned 
about the value of gemstones

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.550
when numbers are more 
important than the memories.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.230
Numbers, huh?

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:24.020
What's wrong with it?

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.690
Seigi-kun, good morning.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:30.180
Good morning, Tanimoto-san.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.820
That's a mineral encyclopedia, isn't it?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.590
Are you into gemstones, Seigi-kun?

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:42.710
I work part-time at a jeweler's. 
Right now, I'm researching heating.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:45.730
Not that you'd care anything about that...

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.690
Heating what kind of gemstone?

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:48.460
Huh?

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:52.210
Beryl? Quartz? Or corundum?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.720
Um, uh... Rubies.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.030
Corundum, then.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:00.310
Rubies and sapphires are called 
corundum in mineralogy.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.160
Oh, sorry!

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:09.150
I was the president of the 
mineralogy club in high school.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.300
It's certainly strange for someone to care

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.970
if a gemstone's been heated or not.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.670
Really?

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:19.950
It can make a gemstone worth 
ten times as much, though.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.060
Wow...

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.690
Wait, that much?

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.350
If they intend to sell it, it makes sense.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.830
The owner said the same thing.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.610
If there's anything I can do 
to help, let me know.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.460
I really appreciate it.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:39.220
I'd love to learn more about gemstones, 
but I don't know where to start.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.350
Gemstones are great.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:45.790
After all, every single gem is one-of-a-kind.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:49.440
There's such romanticism to them, 
regardless of grade.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.360
How cool...

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.170
Huh?

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:56.490
Oh, nothing. You must really like them.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.470
Oh, there I go again.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.320
Once I start talking about 
gemstones, I just can't stop.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:03.330
Sorry.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:07.080
For what? I'd love to hear more.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:08.640
Really?

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.670
Of course.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.130
Thanks.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.800
Then let's chat again sometime. Later!

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:20.810
You forgot to get her number again.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.520
Please, wait!

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.310
I know she came here.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:38.070
Please break it off with Mami-san!

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:47.080
My name is Homura.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.830
Homura 
\hTrading, Ltd. 

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:49.830
I'm sorry for imposing.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.720
Don't worry about it.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:53.700
Now, what can I do for you?

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.390
I'm her fiancé.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:05.600
After everything that's happened, 
I hired someone to investigate her.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.020
Hired someone? You mean a detective?

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.040
I had my reasons.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.770
This won't take long. Please, hear me out.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:19.030
Very well.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.940
Thank you.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:27.230
I met her exactly one year ago.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:28.830
She joined the company in the spring.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.080
I was drawn to how hard-working she was.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:37.780
My parents were delighted, 
and we soon began discussing marriage.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:38.590
But...

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:43.150
It's not working out. 
We haven't gotten anywhere since then.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:48.600
She keeps losing weight, 
and she's stopped smiling.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.490
Maybe it's the marriage blues.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.680
My parents are losing their minds.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:00.970
When I ask her why, 
she won't tell me anything.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.430
I don't know what to do.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:06.520
But you didn't have to hire a detective.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:09.490
There was nothing else I could do!

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:14.160
I'm sorry.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:25.450
Over the past month,
the only thing of interest she's done

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.760
was visit this store.

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.010
I thought she was having an affair with you.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.310
Am I mistaken?

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.020
You are. She just came 
to have a ruby valuated.

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:41.820
A ruby? You mean the brooch I gave her?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:47.690
I don't know about that, 
but I'm sure Akashi-san has her reasons.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.320
Akashi?

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:52.830
Who is Akashi-san?

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.130
This woman.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.000
Her name is Sasu Mami.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.480
Sasu?

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.880
Yes, written with the kanji 
meaning "sandy shoal."

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.190
Her name isn't Akashi Mami-san?

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:11.810
No. Why would she use a fake name?

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.560
<b>Display</b>

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.560
<b>Menu</b>

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.380
Homura-san...

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.740
Let's talk, Mami-san.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:41.590
I don't understand how you feel anymore.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:44.640
Have you fallen in love with someone else?

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:47.510
Is there an old flame you can't forget?

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:53.580
Compared to him, 
I don't think I stand a chance...

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:58.230
But who is it? 
Who does your heart belong to?

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:06.900
Mami-san, I don't care 
if you're having an affair.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.490
No matter who you love, 
I can't give you up.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.700
My feelings will never change.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.080
But it hurts to be left in the dark.

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:26.420
Please tell me. What's troubling you so?

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.030
What's making you so anxious?

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:31.890
What should I do?

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:38.020
Homura-san, I can't marry you.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:49.320
Why not, Mami-san?

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:54.330
That face...

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:02.730
I can't stand growing a vegetable 
garden in a desert anymore.

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:06.800
A vegetable garden in a desert?

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:11.870
Homura-san, this isn't your fault.
 It's entirely mine.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.550
I'm sorry.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.640
Mami-san!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:16.310
Let go!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.270
Seigi.

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:37.110
I'm sorry. You don't need 
to pay me for today.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.210
I had no idea she hated me so much...

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:48.210
This is just a guess, 
but the problem may lie elsewhere.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.720
<b>No Bicycles     Tsukiji Police Department</b>

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.690
<i>Where did she go?</i>

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:10.780
Where should we go next?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.150
Well...

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.240
Look. This bag is so cute.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.990
So then, yesterday...

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:24.460
Mami-san!

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.840
You... Why?

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:37.180
My name is Nakata Seigi, 
as in "hero of justice."

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.810
So I couldn't just look the other way.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:42.050
Hero of justice?

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.340
My grandma named me.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:51.440
And... another woman who's sort
 of like a grandmother to me

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.320
told me to be the kind of person
 who helps those in need.

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:58.320
What does that mean?

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:05.320
My parents raised me 
not to be a bother to others

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:08.530
or draw unnecessary attention to myself.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:15.440
Have a normal wedding, have kids, 
raise them normally, and grow old.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:19.350
They told me that was 
the path to an easy life.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:23.670
I always wanted to follow 
that path, but I can't...

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:27.610
even though Homura-san 
is such a good man.

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.130
Huh?

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:35.540
The person I can't forget...
 is a woman. Akashi Tatsuki.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.620
We lived together for seven years,
up until last year.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.580
So that's what this is about.

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:45.160
It's not normal at all, is it?

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.900
So Akashi was <i>her</i> name.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:53.590
In that case, why did you decide 
to marry Homura-san?

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.600
Living with Tatsuki was hard,

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:59.420
like growing a vegetable garden 
in the middle of the desert.

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:05.750
I wondered why I had to endure 
so much hardship that others didn't.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:10.060
So that's what you meant by a desert...

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:15.410
When I finally decided I wanted 
a normal life, I met Homura-san.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:20.640
But I couldn't sleep, and eventually, 
I couldn't even keep food down.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.370
Our bodies are honest, aren't they?

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:28.710
There's nothing wrong with not 
forcing yourself to get married.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.840
There is.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:34.980
I admire women who live 
happy, ordinary lives.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:38.510
I hate not being one 
so much that I could die.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:40.780
I'm disgusted with myself.

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:47.560
Every gemstone is one-of-a-kind.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:53.570
I doubt there's anyone who always feels
 like they're completely normal.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:57.690
There are some things about 
ourselves we just can't change.

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:05.990
Have you ever thought about becoming
 a counselor, Mr. Hero of Justice?

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:08.680
Mami-san?

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:09.940
Mami-san!

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:16.930
I...

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:22.050
My feelings were making Mami-san suffer.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:34.220
Here are the results of your valuation.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:42.820
It's 3.05 carats, triple A grade, 
originating from Mogok, Myanmar.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:47.330
It's an exceptional unheated gemstone. 
I'd value it around ten million yen.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.000
Ten mill—

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.210
I see.

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:57.960
So... why was it that you really wanted 
to know if it had been heated or not?

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.410
If it was heated, I would marry him.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.840
If not, I would rethink our engagement.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:04.550
Huh?

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:07.890
What? Not the other way around?

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:11.630
I wish he hadn't cared about me.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:14.420
This was supposed to be a rebirth for me.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.470
But with the wedding approaching, 
I got scared for the first time.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.150
I was a mess.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:23.400
I think I wanted someone to tell me that.

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:27.310
Gemstones are mirrors 
that reflect their owners.

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:31.450
They'd never lead you to 
an answer you didn't desire.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:36.550
Perhaps you already had your answer 
when you came here, Sasu-sama.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.960
And I'm the only one who didn't know?

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:44.310
Everyone has their own world.

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:46.760
It's a matter of whether we deny them

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.400
or choose to nurture them as our own.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:59.510
I'll return the brooch to Homura-san.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:07.480
This is good. Thank you.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:17.500
It must be hard for someone 
like Mami-san to live in Japan.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:24.460
Making generalizations by saying 
"people like her" is offensive.

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:26.510
Right, our agreement...

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:31.220
"You will exhibit no prejudice, 
nor speak in a discriminatory manner."

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:34.480
Seigi, how are gemstones measured?

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:35.350
In carats.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.060
Correct.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:42.880
Of course, it's possible to convert 
each carat into 0.2 grams,

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:49.010
but I think a world with many 
different metrics and measures

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:53.810
is easier to live in, 
more beautiful, and much richer.

00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:58.830
I'm going to see our next customer.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.820
Could you make some tea?

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:09.090
All right!
